    "text": "In federated learning, the privacy leakage through gradient inversion can be modeled as a non-Markovian process where the Nakajima-Zwanzig memory kernel quantifies the temporal correlation between global model updates and individual data, with the Laplace transform of the reduced state providing an upper bound on predictability-based fine-grained privacy measures.",
